      }
    },
    "Resonance checks for a new version once a day. Updates are verified with Resonance's signing key before they're installed, and nothing about your Mac is sent. Automatic updates install when you quit." : {

    },
    "Resonance doesn't have the HVSC collection yet." : {

    },
    "Resonance figures out the length of tunes missing from the Songlengths database by itself, in the background. The default length is used until then, and for tunes it can't figure out. 0 means play until silence." : {

    },
    "Resonance hasn't fingerprinted this tune yet." : {

    },
    "Resonance hasn't learned how this tune sounds yet. Try another one, or come back when the scan has reached it." : {

    },
    "Resonance hasn't recorded any crashes." : {
      "comment" : "A description of the state when no crash reports have been recorded.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Resonance hasn't scanned these tunes yet." : {

    },
    "Resonance Help" : {

    },
    "Resonance is in alpha. Report problems on GitHub, from Help → Report a Problem, with what you did and what happened." : {

    },
    "Resonance is still %@ after the update tried to install. You can download the new version from the website." : {

    },
    "Resonance keeps its favorites, play history, playlists, fingerprints and, unless you choose another folder, HVSC in its own folder." : {

    },
    "Resonance measures up to three minutes of each tune, by watching what it asks the SID chip to do. It draws nine of those measurements as a **barcode** in tune lists and as a **sphere** on the Sounds Like card and the barcode's hover card." : {

    },
    "Resonance only answers on your Mac, but what your assistant reads, such as playlist names and what you've played, goes wherever that assistant sends what you ask it." : {

    },
    "Resonance plays Commodore 64 music: SID tunes, through the emulation engine of Phosphor, an open-source SID player. Its library is the High Voltage SID Collection (HVSC), about 60,000 tunes by thousands of composers." : {

    },
    "Resonance plays every tune in the collection silently in the background and learns how it sounds: its waveforms, its arpeggios and filter sweeps, its drums and its bass. That fingerprint is what it compares, across all of HVSC, along with an embedding of each tune's sound, made in advance and downloaded once." : {

    },
    "Resonance plays every tune silently in the background to learn how it sounds, for the Fingerprint column and Sounds Like. It picks up where it left off, and takes a few hours for all of HVSC. The published set (about 42 MB) has the fingerprints of all of HVSC already; Resonance downloads it the first time, and the scan fills in the rest." : {

    },
    "Resonance plays tunes from HVSC, the High Voltage SID Collection. Download it (it's free) to play this tune." : {

    },
    "Resonance quit unexpectedly." : {
      "comment" : "The title of the issue in GitHub.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
    "Resonance shows what's playing in Control Center, with the tune's fingerprint sphere as its picture, or its composer's colors before it's scanned, and answers your keyboard's play, next and previous keys. Control Center's position slider and its 15-second skips work too." : {

    },
    "Resonance Website" : {

    },
    "Resonance would contact csdb.dk, a site we don't run: to fetch the news, look up composers you open, and download CSDb tunes you play. If you say no, it never does. You can change this in Settings." : {

    },
    "Resonance's command line tool can serve the Model Context Protocol, so an assistant can search, play, make playlists, open HVSC's own playlists and start a drift. Then you can ask for “something like Commando but darker”, or who on HVSC Favorite Top 100 still makes music." : {

    },
