    "System Settings" : {

    },
    "The **#** column shows each tune's place in the playlist." : {

    },
    "The **Fingerprint** column shows each tune's fingerprint as a barcode. Hover it for a card with the tune's sphere and sound, to play it or find similar tunes." : {

    },
    "The **Resonance** extension is coming soon to the Raycast Store. It doesn't need the command line tool, and if Resonance isn't running, it starts in the background." : {

    },
    "The **Sound** chips above a list keep only the tunes that have all the sounds you pick: Arpeggios, Filter sweeps, Noise drums, Ring mod, Sync leads and Digi samples." : {

    },
    "The %@ engine can't scrub. Click for why." : {

    },
    "The %@ engine plays a tune in real time only, so there's nothing to jump to. The reSIDfp and SIDLite direct engines run the tune to the point you choose." : {

    },
    "The acknowledgments are missing from this build." : {

    },
    "The bar at the bottom" : {

    },
    "The barcode" : {

    },
    "The barcode and the sphere show only part of what Sounds Like compares: 41 measurements of how a tune drives the chip, and an embedding of its sound. Two tunes can look alike and still not be close matches, or the other way around. The percentage on a match is the better guide." : {

    },
    "The C64 scene still releases music. CSDb is its database. Turn this on for Scene Pulse, with new releases and parties, and for composers' groups and credits." : {

    },
    "The card at the top of the inspector has three pages. Swipe between them on a trackpad, or click the dots along its bottom edge; Resonance remembers the last one." : {

    },
    "The chip button in the player bar, or **View → Show Under the Hood**, slides a drawer up over the list, and the button at its top right slides it back down." : {

    },
    "The collection couldn't be read. Try again." : {

    },
    "The collection has finished downloading." : {

    },
    "The colors group the bars: cyan for pitch movement, violet for the filter, orange for the chip's harsher sounds, red for samples and green for pulse width. Notes take the color of the text." : {

    },
    "The column on the right (toggle it with **Inspector** in the toolbar) shows what's playing: the voices of the chip, Sounds Like, the tune's details, STIL's notes and stories about it, its composer, and HVSC's known bugs when the tune has any. Where the tune came from — “Playing from Rob Hubbard” — is a link back to it." : {

    },
    "The controls on the Dock icon, and word when something long ends." : {

    },
    "The dark side: saber red" : {

    },
    "The Describe row in the sidebar makes a Smart Playlist from a sentence, or from New to Me, Never Heard, Similar to a Tune and Slow to Intense. It reads sentences just as the app does, and the app's Smart Playlist pane follows along. **Return** plays from a tune, **/** changes the sentence, **n** saves the list as a playlist and **Esc** starts over." : {

    },
